      "content": "1. Definition of Tense"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Tenses indicate the time of action and are broadly divided into Present, Past, and Future.",
        "Each primary tense contains four aspects: Simple, Continuous, Perfect, and Perfect Continuous.",
        "Mastering all 12 tense structures is fundamental for solving error detection and sentence improvement questions.",
        "Competitive exam questions heavily focus on subject-verb alignment and time-bound adverbial triggers."
      ],
      "id": "z6iod3a"
