    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Simple Past vs. Present Perfect: Use Simple Past when explicit past time adverbs (e.g., 'yesterday', 'in 1947', 'ago') are present.",
        "Past Perfect Rule: When two past actions occur sequentially, use Past Perfect for the earlier action and Simple Past for the later one.",
        "Stative Verbs: Verbs of perception, emotion, and possession (e.g., 'know', 'love', 'belong') are generally not used in Continuous Tenses."
      ],
      "id": "5tuw6pd"
    },
